. sg. अर्दय, impf. आ॑दयत्, 2. sg. आर्द॑यस्; aor. आर्दिदत्, or [after मा] अर्दयीत्, Pāṇ. iii, 1, 51)
to make agitated, stir up, shake vehemently, AV. iv, 15, 6 & 11; vi, 49, 2, to do harm, torment, distress, MBh. &c. (generally used in perf. Pass. p. अर्दित, q.v.),
to strike, hurt, kill, destroy, RV.; AV. &c. Desid. अर्दिदिषति;

